  "body": "### Summary\nAs a user updating from HFR+, I want the first-launch import (LOT-158) to show a small illustrated construction worker while it runs, so that the wait feels intended and friendly instead of a bare spinner (operator, 2026-11-10).\n\n### Today\n`App/SwiftHFR/RootView.swift:22` shows a progress view while `LegacyImportModel.isRunning` (LOT-158, #720, merged as ddcbf25); the \"Import de HFR+\" summary sheet follows (kept as is, operator OK 2026-11-10).\n\n### Scope\n- An original drawing of a small construction worker (helmet, tools), in the app's illustration style 1 « digital sketching » (`docs/THEMES.md` §6: flat colour areas, little shading, contours as the boards). **Original work only**: no existing mascot or character. The art is made by a committed script (SVG source), with light and dark variants, readable at 64 pt.\n- Two variants, both rendered as previews in the PR so the operator chooses:\n  - **A, animated character**: one simple loop, e.g. the hammer taps or the shovel digs (2–4 parts moved by SwiftUI, no frame sequence);\n  - **B, static character and a loading animation**: the drawing plus a progress indicator next to it (a turning gear or a dashed progress line).\n- Text under it: « Import de vos données HFR+… » (French, short), and the step being imported if the model exposes it (counts only, never a pseudo).\n- Reduce Motion: no motion, the static drawing plus a standard progress indicator. VoiceOver: one label and the progress value, the drawing hidden from accessibility.\n- No new dependency (no Lottie): SwiftUI shapes or an SVG in the asset catalogue.\n\n### Acceptance criteria\n- The preview images of A and B (light and dark) are committed under the PR's `docs/assets/` folder and shown in the PR body; the operator picks one, and the other is removed before the merge.\n- Swift Testing: the import view shows the animation while running, and the static form under Reduce Motion.\n- Mac check: an iPhone first launch over a legacy install, in light and dark, with Reduce Motion on and off.\n\nM4 (follows LOT-158; an operator design choice, hence `origin: deliberate-gap`). Credit: the art's maker in CREDITS.md, as THEMES.md §6.5.\n\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
